From: MOSS Windows lane <moss@example.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The delete-child deny on a denied target's parent, on the parent alone

---

Upstream: anthropics/sandbox-runtime, tag v0.0.81 (c40cf14), after 0001-0003.
Reason: every deny srt-win stamps also puts a FILE_DELETE_CHILD deny on the
target's parent, inheritable (OI|CI). Writing an inheritable entry makes the
system walk everything below the object to bring its inherited entries up to
date, so a target at the top of a profile walks the whole profile, at stamp
and again at restore: measured on windows-latest, one deny on a new folder at
the top of a 50,829-entry profile took 21-27 s, one a level down 0.2-0.4 s,
with or without the profile read grant. The delete-child check that protects
the target is made on its parent object alone, so the parent's entry need not
be handed down; on the parent alone it changes nothing objects below inherit,
and srt-win's own writer (`commit_dacl`, `same_inheritable`) writes the
parent's list on the object without the walk.

What the inherited entry also did: it kept FILE_DELETE_CHILD denied on the
target and everything below it. A read deny (FILE_ALL) denies that right
itself; a write deny's mask holds DELETE but not FILE_DELETE_CHILD, and a
delete is granted by the parent's FILE_DELETE_CHILD whatever the child's own
DELETE says. So a write deny now carries its own inheritable delete-child deny
on the target: written with the target's deny, it walks only the target's own
tree, which that deny walks already.

Files: src/acl.rs.

What changes, and nothing else, per session (`SbAceSet::aces`) and persistent
(`persistent_aces`): the parent's FILE_DELETE_CHILD deny is written without
OI|CI; a write-denied target gains `(D;OICI;FILE_DELETE_CHILD)`. Two unit tests
of the persistent shape follow.

diff --git a/src/acl.rs b/src/acl.rs
--- a/src/acl.rs
+++ b/src/acl.rs
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 //!   sandbox user (which has no inherent rights on real-user-owned
 //!   files) can reach the working tree;
 //! - `stamp` ⇒ `(D;OICI;mask;;;<sb-SID>)` on the target plus
-//!   `(D;OICI;FILE_DELETE_CHILD;;;<sb-SID>)` on the parent;
+//!   `(D;;FILE_DELETE_CHILD;;;<sb-SID>)` on the parent, object only (MOSS patch 0004);
 //! - install-time ambient write-denies (`ambient.rs`) reuse the
 //!   `stamp` deny shape, recorded in `ambient_denies` with no holder
 //!   so they persist across sessions until `uninstall`.
@@ -973,7 +973,7 @@
 pub enum SbAce {
     Grant(GrantMask),
     Deny(DenyMask),
-    /// `(D;OICI;FILE_DELETE_CHILD;;;<sb>)` — applied to the parent
+    /// `(D;;FILE_DELETE_CHILD;;;<sb>)` (object only, MOSS patch 0004) — applied to the parent
     /// of every denied target so the sandbox user cannot `del`/`ren`
     /// it via parent-FDC even when the parent carries an inherited
     /// `BUILTIN\Users:(F)` (which the sandbox user, a Users member,
@@ -1088,12 +1088,24 @@
         let mut v = Vec::with_capacity(3);
         if let Some(m) = self.deny {
             v.push(NewAce::Deny(sid, m.bits(), OICI));
+        }
+        // MOSS patch 0004: a write deny's own delete-child deny, on the target and all below
+        // it. The write mask holds DELETE but not FILE_DELETE_CHILD, and a delete is granted
+        // by the parent's FILE_DELETE_CHILD whatever the child's own DELETE says; what below
+        // the target kept that right denied was the parent's entry, inherited. It is the
+        // target's own now (the read deny, FILE_ALL, holds it already).
+        if self.deny == Some(DenyMask::WriteDeny) {
+            v.push(NewAce::Deny(sid, Mask::FILE_DELETE_CHILD.bits(), OICI));
         }
         if self.deny_delete {
             v.push(NewAce::Deny(sid, Mask::DELETE.bits(), NO_INHERIT));
         }
+        // MOSS patch 0004: the parent's delete-child deny on the parent ALONE (`NO_INHERIT`):
+        // what protects the target is that check on its parent object. Inheritable, the entry
+        // went to every object below the parent and writing it walked that whole tree (a target
+        // at a profile's top: the profile, ~50,000 entries, 21-27 s at stamp and at restore).
         if self.deny_fdc {
-            v.push(NewAce::Deny(sid, Mask::FILE_DELETE_CHILD.bits(), OICI));
+            v.push(NewAce::Deny(sid, Mask::FILE_DELETE_CHILD.bits(), NO_INHERIT));
         }
         let allow = self
             .grant
@@ -1493,13 +1505,18 @@
     let mut v = Vec::with_capacity(7);
     if let Some(m) = w.deny {
         v.push(AceView::explicit(true, g, m.bits(), OICI));
+    }
+    // MOSS patch 0004: as the per-session set ([`SbAceSet::aces`]): a write deny's own
+    // delete-child deny, inheritable; the parent's, on the parent alone.
+    let fdc = Mask::FILE_DELETE_CHILD.bits();
+    if w.deny == Some(DenyMask::WriteDeny) {
+        v.push(AceView::explicit(true, g, fdc, OICI));
     }
     if w.deny_delete {
         v.push(AceView::explicit(true, g, Mask::DELETE.bits(), NO_INHERIT));
     }
     if w.deny_fdc {
-        let fdc = Mask::FILE_DELETE_CHILD.bits();
-        v.push(AceView::explicit(true, g, fdc, OICI));
+        v.push(AceView::explicit(true, g, fdc, NO_INHERIT));
     }
     if let Some(cap) = w.capability_sid {
         let modify = Mask::MODIFY_NO_FDC.bits();
@@ -1820,8 +1837,9 @@
             sddl,
             [
                 format!("(D;OICI;{:#x};;;{GROUP})", DenyMask::WriteDeny.bits()),
-                format!("(D;;0x10000;;;{GROUP})"),
                 format!("(D;OICI;0x40;;;{GROUP})"),
+                format!("(D;;0x10000;;;{GROUP})"),
+                format!("(D;;0x40;;;{GROUP})"),
             ]
         );
         let both = persistent_aces(&PersistentWant {
@@ -2069,6 +2087,7 @@
             list(Some(ProfileAce::Granted), Some(DenyMask::WriteDeny), None),
             [
                 format!("(D;OICI;{:#x};;;{GROUP})", DenyMask::WriteDeny.bits()),
+                format!("(D;OICI;0x40;;;{GROUP})"),
                 format!("(A;OICI;0x1200a9;;;{GROUP})"),
             ]
         );
